# EV Dashboard using STM32

This project demonstrates the design and implementation of an Embedded EV Dashboard using the STM32 microcontroller. The dashboard monitors and displays important electric vehicle parameters and provides a simple simulation of vehicle status.

## Project Overview

The objective of this project is to understand embedded system development using STM32 by designing a dashboard capable of monitoring basic EV parameters.

## Features

- Vehicle speed display
- Battery level monitoring
- Temperature monitoring
- Distance/Range indication
- Real-time dashboard simulation
- Embedded C implementation using STM32

## Hardware Used

- STM32 Blue Pill (STM32F103C8T6)
- LEDs
- Potentiometers
- Push Buttons
- Ultrasonic Sensors(3)
- Breadboard
- Jumper Wires

## Software & Tools

- STM32CubeIDE
- Python (for dashboard)
- VSPE
- Picsimlab
- Embedded C
- STM32 HAL Library
- GitHub

## Project Files

This folder contains:

- Source Code
- STM32 Project Files
- Python code

## Learning Outcomes

Through this project, I learned:

- STM32 programming
- GPIO configuration
- ADC interfacing
- Embedded C programming
- Debugging embedded applications
- Embedded dashboard development

This project was developed as part of my Electronics and Communication Engineering (ECE) learning and is intended for educational and internship portfolio purposes.